# Backend architecture

## Modular structure

- **Organization by modules** - code organized in `Web.Api/Modules/{ModuleName}/`
- **Module structure**:
  - `Controllers/` - API controllers
  - `Dtos/` - Data Transfer Objects
  - `Handlers/` - command and query handlers (CQRS)

Example structure:
```
Modules/
└─ Vacancies/
   ├─ Controllers/
   │  └─ VacanciesController.cs
   ├─ Dtos/
   │  └─ SubmitResumeDto.cs
   └─ Handlers/
      └─ Create
      │  └─ SubmitResumeCommand.cs
      │  └─ SubmitResumeCommandHandler.cs
      │  └─ SubmitResumeCommandValidator.cs
      └─ Read
         └─ GetByIdQuery.cs
         └─ GetByIdQueryHandler.cs
         └─ GetByIdQueryValidator.cs
```

## CQRS with MediatR

- **Separate commands and queries** - use separate classes for commands (data changes) and queries (reads)
- **Handlers** - all business logic in handlers, not in controllers
- **MediatR usage** - all interaction via `IMediator.Send()` and `IMediator.Send<T>()`

Example command:
```csharp
public class SubmitResumeCommand : Command<bool>
{
    public SubmitResumeDto Dto { get; set; }
}

public class SubmitResumeCommandHandler : CommandHandler<SubmitResumeCommand, bool>
{
    protected override async Task<bool> HandleAsync(SubmitResumeCommand command, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        // Business logic
        return true;
    }
}
```

## DTOs

- **Separate DTOs** - use separate classes for requests and responses
- **Validation** - use FluentValidation for DTO validation
- **Naming** - `Dto` suffix for all DTOs

Example:
```csharp
public class SubmitResumeDto
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public string Email { get; set; }
    public string Phone { get; set; }
    public IFormFile Resume { get; set; }
}
```

## Dependency Injection

- **Constructor injection** - use constructor for dependency injection
- **Interfaces** - use interfaces for all dependencies
- **Readonly fields** - all dependencies must be `readonly`

Example:
```csharp
public class VacanciesController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IMediator _mediator;
    private readonly ILogger<VacanciesController> _logger;

    public VacanciesController(
        IMediator mediator,
        ILogger<VacanciesController> logger)
    {
        _mediator = mediator;
        _logger = logger;
    }
}
```
